# Before tagging a release: add the paper's DOI, volume, and page numbers under
# preferred-citation, and confirm the author list matches the manuscript.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use PrinTE in your research, please cite the paper below.
title: "PrinTE: a forward simulator of transposable-element genome evolution"
abstract: >-
  PrinTE evolves a genome one generation at a time, repeatedly mutating the DNA,
  inserting new transposable elements and excising old ones, with realistic nesting,
  solo-LTR formation, cut-and-paste and copy-and-paste transposition, selection against
  gene disruption, and chromatin bias.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Benson
    given-names: Chris
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3752-6378"
repository-code: https://github.com/cwb14/PrinTE
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - transposable elements
  - genome evolution
  - forward simulation
  - LTR retrotransposon
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "PrinTE: a forward simulator of transposable-element genome evolution"
  authors:
